      "id": "at-glance",
      "title": "At a glance",
      "body": "For travelers, Tôi có đặt chỗ is the phrase to keep ready for \"I have a booking\" in times, dates, tickets, waits, and bookings. This is for when the booking exists and you need staff to find it first. Start with the booking before you ask about timing changes. It works best when you focus on putting the booking first so staff can look it up before you explain more. After you say it, listen for a name check, booking-code request, counter direction, or short wait; the next rows help you keep the exchange moving.",
